- The too-short warning now appears on step 1, next to the dates, with a **Continue anyway** button. If you change the dates after seeing it, it warns again.\n\n**2. Plan summary page.** After the last step you land on the summary instead of the calendar. Each plan on the Plans page also has a **Summary** button, and its title links there too. The page shows:\n- **Goal:** race and distance, race date, number of weeks, start date.\n- **Schedule:** run days and long-run day.\n- **The plan at a glance:** starting week, peak week, longest run and total km. These come from the plan's actual runs, so they reflect any runs you've edited. Two choices I made:\n  - Weekly figures leave out the race itself, so race week doesn't show up as the peak.\n  - \"Starting week\" is the first full week, because week 1 is partial when a plan starts mid-week.\n- **Race day estimate**, which works like this:\n  - **\"Best\" recent race:** races of different lengths can't be compared directly, so I take the one that predicts the fastest time for your goal race. For example, a 24:30 5K beats a 1:58:00 half when predicting a half. \"Your speed now\" is that race's pace per km.\n  - **Finish range:** the slow end is Riegel's prediction for today; the fast end is 3% faster, for the effect of training.\n  - **Target pace:** the middle of that range, per km. I didn't want to set the target at the optimistic end.\n  - **Short-race caveat:** if the race is much shorter than the goal (like a 5K for a marathon), the page says the estimate is less reliable.\n  - **No race times:** it says \"An estimated finish time needs a recent race time\", with a link to edit the plan.\n- **Button:** \"Go to calendar\". For a plan that isn't active, it's \"Make active and go to calendar\".\n\nI checked the maths by hand: a 24:30 5K gives a 10K estimate of 49:33 – 51:05 and a target pace of 5:02 /km. It lives in a new file, `estimates.py`, kept separate like `plan.py`.\n\n**3. Top bar:** it now shows Calendar, Plans, Profile, your username and Log out. The app name is no longer a link, so \"Calendar\" is the only link back. The Week/Month switch on the calendar works as before.\n\nThe database didn't change, so your existing accounts and plans keep working, and their summary pages are available now. Your real data in `instance/` wasn't touched by testing. The README is updated.","ttft_ms":25140,"type":"result","duration_ms":187539,"uuid":"053133c7-b070-489e-9fa7-878d5181cf0d","ttft_stream_ms":1893,"time_to_request_ms":99,"first_content_frame_ms":1893,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
